{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban Isolation as a sanction in schools",
        "additional_details": "Schools can use isolation (reflection or seclusion) as a punishment, placing 11-16 year olds in silent rooms with side partitions and limited toilet breaks. We are concerned that for some students this could cause severe distress and lasting damage including:\r\n \r\nChronic Anxiety & Panic: Triggering ongoing anxiety disorders and panic attacks in structured settings.\r\nDepression & Apathy: Clinical depression, loss of pleasure, and a feeling that effort is meaningless.",
        "background": "The isolation sanction, which is widely used in schools, should be banned and replaced with something more effective and less psychologically distressing for students.",
